__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
# Agent worktrees are live workspaces, not content — committing one would land
# in-progress, unverified work alongside a nested git checkout.
.claude/worktrees/
# Hypothesis's example database (tests/test_properties.py). Deliberately not
# committed: CI must *derive* its counterexamples from the properties, not
# replay a file somebody's laptop wrote — a checked-in database would make a
# green run depend on which examples happened to be cached, which is the same
# reproducibility claim `--replay` makes about a corpus.
.hypothesis/
# The default vector cache (`worldloom evaluate --retriever embedding`, see
# `src/worldloom/evaluate/embedding.py`). A *corpus's* cache is meant to be
# carried and committed — that is what makes a dense measurement replay without
# the model — but this is the scratch one a working tree accumulates while
# scoring whatever happened to be to hand, keyed to no corpus in particular.
# Point `--vectors` at the corpus to keep one worth keeping.
.worldloom/
# Managed AlphaEvolve credentials and controller scratch belong to the local
# operator. Dated, reviewed result receipts under evals/alphaevolve remain
# commit-worthy; raw controller state does not.
.alphaevolve.env
evals/_runs/
